(version 1)

# JLCPCB baseline custom design rules — shared starting point for every
# KiCad board in this project. Copy into a new project as
# <board>.kicad_dru, then retune the RF width band against the stackup
# actually being fabbed.
#
# See kicad_jlcpcb_design_rules.md §5.3. KiCad has no live binding between
# the impedance profile and the stackup, so the width below is computed
# once by hand and pinned here; this rule is what makes DRC flag a trace
# that drifts off it.
#
# Width band assumes JLCPCB JLC04161H-7628, 4-layer 1.6 mm, L1 over a
# solid L2 ground plane, 50 ohm microstrip ~0.358 mm. Recompute with the
# JLCPCB impedance calculator if the stackup changes.

(rule "RF 50ohm microstrip width"
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'RF'")
  (constraint track_width (min 0.35mm) (opt 0.358mm) (max 0.37mm)))
